WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.259 --> 00:00:07.362
♪♪

00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:09.197
&gt;&gt;&gt; In our health lead today, a

00:00:09.331 --> 00:00:11.166
hearing in the biggest

00:00:11.299 --> 00:00:12.601
abortion-related case since the

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:15.403
U.S. Supreme court overturned

00:00:15.737 --> 00:00:16.905
roe V. Wade, depending upon how

00:00:17.038 --> 00:00:19.274
a trump-appointed judge in Texas

00:00:19.407 --> 00:00:20.575
handles this lawsuit.

00:00:20.709 --> 00:00:23.378
Access to the most common method

00:00:23.745 --> 00:00:26.114
of abortion, pills, could be cut

00:00:26.248 --> 00:00:27.816
off nationwide.

00:00:27.949 --> 00:00:30.151
CNN's Rosa flores explains how

00:00:30.285 --> 00:00:31.753
this could happen even in states

00:00:31.753 --> 00:00:33.755
where abortion is perfectly

00:00:33.755 --> 00:00:33.855
legal.

00:00:33.989 --> 00:00:35.156
&gt;&gt; Reporter: The national

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:36.858
abortion debate, heating in a

00:00:36.992 --> 00:00:38.627
federal courthouse in Amarillo,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:39.127
Texas.

00:00:39.261 --> 00:00:40.662
Inside, the biggest legal battle

00:00:40.795 --> 00:00:43.198
over abortion since the supreme

00:00:43.331 --> 00:00:45.100
court overturned roe V. Wade.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.269
A federal judge is seriously

00:00:47.402 --> 00:00:51.840
considering undoing fda approval

00:00:51.973 --> 00:00:54.376
of mifepristone, an abortion

00:00:54.509 --> 00:00:55.076
medication available for more

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.145
than two decades in a lawsuit

00:00:57.279 --> 00:00:58.914
brought by an anti-abortion

00:00:59.047 --> 00:00:59.281
coalition.

00:00:59.414 --> 00:01:02.284
&gt;&gt; The impact in overruling the

00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:05.387
fda's approval of mifepristone

00:01:05.787 --> 00:01:06.755
is far reaching.

00:01:06.888 --> 00:01:08.156
Doctors and patients will not

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.358
know if we can trust the

00:01:10.492 --> 00:01:11.927
national guidelines which tell

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.062
us to follow the standard of

00:01:14.195 --> 00:01:14.362
care.

00:01:14.496 --> 00:01:15.797
&gt;&gt; Reporter: During the

00:01:15.897 --> 00:01:16.865
four-hour preliminary injunction

00:01:16.998 --> 00:01:19.000
hearing the judge raised one

00:01:19.134 --> 00:01:20.669
possible scenario where he could

00:01:20.802 --> 00:01:24.472
keep the drug's approval intact,

00:01:24.606 --> 00:01:26.141
and instead block the fda's

00:01:26.274 --> 00:01:28.710
rules to make it easier to

00:01:28.843 --> 00:01:29.044
obtain.

00:01:29.177 --> 00:01:30.679
&gt;&gt; It's a 20-year-old drug

00:01:30.812 --> 00:01:32.714
actually used to save women's

00:01:32.847 --> 00:01:33.014
lives.

00:01:33.148 --> 00:01:34.416
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Legal concerns

00:01:34.549 --> 00:01:36.418
always restricting access.

00:01:36.551 --> 00:01:39.821
Walgreens plans to stop the sale

00:01:39.821 --> 00:01:41.423
of the pill after states

00:01:41.823 --> 00:01:42.390
threatened to sue.

00:01:42.524 --> 00:01:43.858
In this case, the plaintiffs are

00:01:43.992 --> 00:01:45.360
arguing the drug is unsafe.

00:01:45.493 --> 00:01:47.262
And the fda's approval process

00:01:47.395 --> 00:01:48.063
was flawed.

00:01:48.196 --> 00:01:49.831
The women's March and other

00:01:49.965 --> 00:01:53.835
abortion advocacy groups say the

00:01:53.835 --> 00:01:55.837
plaintiffs went, quote, judge

00:01:55.904 --> 00:01:57.439
shopping for someone they

00:01:57.839 --> 00:02:00.675
believe will rule in their

00:02:00.809 --> 00:02:00.976
favor.

00:02:01.109 --> 00:02:04.512
There's one federal judge,

00:02:04.646 --> 00:02:06.147
Matthew Kaczmarek, a president

00:02:06.281 --> 00:02:08.950
trump appointee who went working

00:02:09.084 --> 00:02:10.885
on anti-abortion advocacy to the

00:02:11.019 --> 00:02:11.853
federal bench.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.521
&gt;&gt; It would be unprecedented for

00:02:13.855 --> 00:02:15.857
a judge, a single judge, to say

00:02:15.857 --> 00:02:17.859
the fda got it wrong 23 years

00:02:17.859 --> 00:02:17.892
ago.

00:02:18.026 --> 00:02:19.961
There's never been an instance

00:02:20.095 --> 00:02:22.364
where anyone has overturned the

00:02:22.497 --> 00:02:24.399
rooming of the fda against the

00:02:24.532 --> 00:02:26.368
fda wishes.

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:28.670
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Judge kacsmaryk's

00:02:28.803 --> 00:02:31.272
hearing had been shrouded in

00:02:31.406 --> 00:02:34.476
secrecy, the judge saying he

00:02:34.609 --> 00:02:37.412
didn't want to out of security

00:02:37.545 --> 00:02:37.979
concerns.

00:02:38.113 --> 00:02:41.883
Sparking outrage over lack of

00:02:42.017 --> 00:02:42.317
transparency.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:43.485
&gt;&gt; I'm dressed like a clown to

00:02:43.885 --> 00:02:45.887
show what a circus he's created.

00:02:45.887 --> 00:02:46.621
It's just a joke.

00:02:46.755 --> 00:02:48.556
He's making the American court

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:50.191
system into a circus.

00:02:50.325 --> 00:02:50.925
&gt;&gt; Reporter: More than half of

00:02:51.059 --> 00:02:54.062
the abortions in the U.S. In

00:02:54.195 --> 00:02:57.532
recent years were medication

00:02:57.899 --> 00:02:59.901
abortions most using

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:00.301
mifepristone.

00:03:00.435 --> 00:03:02.037
&gt;&gt; And mifepristone is not just

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:04.372
used in abortion care, it's also

00:03:04.506 --> 00:03:06.007
used for miscarriage management.

00:03:06.141 --> 00:03:07.909
&gt;&gt; Reporter: The judge didn't

00:03:07.909 --> 00:03:08.943
rule from the bench today.

00:03:09.077 --> 00:03:10.845
And said he'd issue an opinion

00:03:10.979 --> 00:03:12.180
as soon as possible.

00:03:12.313 --> 00:03:14.616
Now, about what could be in that

00:03:14.749 --> 00:03:16.251
opinion, in the judge's

00:03:16.384 --> 00:03:18.653
questioning, he hinted at being

00:03:18.787 --> 00:03:19.921
sympathetic towards the legal

00:03:19.921 --> 00:03:22.724
arguments of the plaintiffs.

00:03:22.857 --> 00:03:25.927
But and this nuance is

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.095
important, in his many

00:03:27.228 --> 00:03:29.330
questions, he also showed some

00:03:29.464 --> 00:03:30.532
skepticism towards granting an

00:03:30.665 --> 00:03:31.933
order that would be as

00:03:31.933 --> 00:03:32.567
aggressive as the plaintiffs

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:33.334
would want.

00:03:33.468 --> 00:03:33.935
Jake.

00:03:33.935 --> 00:03:37.338
&gt;&gt; All right, Rosa flores, in

00:03:37.472 --> 00:03:38.306
Amarillo, Texas.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.709
Let's bring in Katie Watson an

00:03:40.842 --> 00:03:45.113
associate professor of

00:03:45.246 --> 00:03:48.316
obstetrics and gynecology at

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:48.750
northwestern.

00:03:48.883 --> 00:03:49.951
She's also an attorney.

00:03:49.951 --> 00:03:52.153
If the plaintiffs, a group of

00:03:52.287 --> 00:03:54.289
docks, medical associations that

00:03:54.422 --> 00:03:56.891
oppose abortion, if they do get

00:03:57.025 --> 00:03:59.094
this preliminary injunction, it

00:03:59.227 --> 00:04:01.229
would forcing the fda, correct

00:04:01.362 --> 00:04:04.065
me if I'm wrong, to withdrew the

00:04:04.199 --> 00:04:05.967
approval of the drug

00:04:05.967 --> 00:04:08.002
mifepristone, while his lawsuit

00:04:08.136 --> 00:04:08.937
playing out.

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:11.973
How would this theoretically

00:04:11.973 --> 00:04:13.641
affect women in the country

00:04:13.975 --> 00:04:15.009
practically speaking?

00:04:15.143 --> 00:04:17.979
&gt;&gt; I think the impact is not

00:04:17.979 --> 00:04:18.113
theoretical.

00:04:18.246 --> 00:04:20.882
We know over half of people

00:04:21.015 --> 00:04:22.951
choosing abortion choose

00:04:23.084 --> 00:04:24.385
medication abortion.

00:04:24.519 --> 00:04:25.386
In two-thirds.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:26.621
United States where abortion is

00:04:26.755 --> 00:04:28.256
legal, it would remove this

00:04:28.389 --> 00:04:29.991
popular method of abortion.

00:04:29.991 --> 00:04:31.993
So, essentially this is

00:04:31.993 --> 00:04:32.727
anti-abortion plaintiffs trying

00:04:32.861 --> 00:04:34.095
to control the choices of people

00:04:34.229 --> 00:04:34.996
who live in states where

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:40.602
abortion is legal.

00:04:40.735 --> 00:04:43.505
And it would absolutely

00:04:43.638 --> 00:04:45.373
unprecedented dramatic overreach

00:04:45.507 --> 00:04:48.009
to have a federal judge tell the

00:04:48.009 --> 00:04:48.843
fda what to do.

00:04:48.977 --> 00:04:50.712
&gt;&gt; It is interesting because

00:04:50.845 --> 00:04:52.747
we've heard a lot of

00:04:52.881 --> 00:04:54.015
anti-abortion leerl scholars

00:04:54.082 --> 00:04:55.650
after overturn of roe V. Wade,

00:04:56.017 --> 00:04:57.485
well this is going to kick it

00:04:57.619 --> 00:04:58.887
back to the states and that's

00:04:59.020 --> 00:04:59.687
where it belongs.

00:05:00.021 --> 00:05:02.157
You're saying this would be much

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:03.324
more aggressive than that?

00:05:03.458 --> 00:05:05.226
&gt;&gt; No, this completely counters

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:06.161
that fabrication.

00:05:06.294 --> 00:05:08.196
The idea is to control abortion

00:05:08.329 --> 00:05:08.596
nationally.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:10.498
And when these plaintiffs say

00:05:10.632 --> 00:05:12.767
that medication causes harm, as

00:05:12.967 --> 00:05:15.069
a medical ethicist, I'll tell

00:05:15.203 --> 00:05:17.438
you, I think what they mean,

00:05:17.572 --> 00:05:20.041
they perceive all abortion as a

00:05:20.041 --> 00:05:20.909
sort of moral harm.

00:05:21.042 --> 00:05:23.244
But that's not how the fda works

00:05:23.378 --> 00:05:27.682
or what science is based on.

00:05:28.049 --> 00:05:34.088
So they've made speechous claims

00:05:34.222 --> 00:05:34.823
to the court.

00:05:34.956 --> 00:05:36.558
&gt;&gt; Let's talk about the women

00:05:36.691 --> 00:05:37.725
that live in the 31 state where

00:05:38.059 --> 00:05:40.061
is this kind of medication

00:05:40.161 --> 00:05:42.063
abortion is legal.

00:05:42.063 --> 00:05:43.598
And if suddenly it's made

00:05:43.731 --> 00:05:45.333
illegal and women can't get it,

00:05:45.466 --> 00:05:46.868
and girls can't get it and they

00:05:47.001 --> 00:05:49.304
need to get an abortion for

00:05:49.437 --> 00:05:50.705
whatever reason, what would

00:05:50.839 --> 00:05:51.372
these women do?

00:05:51.506 --> 00:05:52.774
&gt;&gt; Well, let's be clear about

00:05:52.907 --> 00:05:54.108
what's on the table and what we

00:05:54.242 --> 00:05:55.043
don't know.

00:05:55.176 --> 00:05:57.145
So, this case specifically

00:05:57.278 --> 00:05:59.380
targets a drug called

00:05:59.514 --> 00:06:00.148
mifepristone which is the first

00:06:00.281 --> 00:06:02.717
of two drugs used in a

00:06:02.851 --> 00:06:04.319
medication abortion regiment.

00:06:04.452 --> 00:06:06.321
And so, it's possible that a

00:06:06.454 --> 00:06:10.959
ruling would still have the drug

00:06:11.092 --> 00:06:13.261
that's been on the market and

00:06:13.394 --> 00:06:14.696
stalked in pharmacies and been

00:06:14.829 --> 00:06:16.197
around for decades.

00:06:16.331 --> 00:06:18.299
And so people could in those

00:06:18.433 --> 00:06:21.603
states where abortion is

00:06:21.736 --> 00:06:26.341
generally legal do that only

00:06:26.474 --> 00:06:26.774
regiment.

00:06:26.908 --> 00:06:30.111
Which is my understanding is 5%

00:06:30.111 --> 00:06:33.448
or 10% less effective, and much

00:06:33.581 --> 00:06:34.515
less comfortable for the

00:06:34.649 --> 00:06:35.316
patient.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:38.786
A two-drug standard is really

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.989
the gold standard.

00:06:41.122 --> 00:06:44.659
It's possible that people will

00:06:44.792 --> 00:06:46.594
go with that or a procedural

00:06:46.728 --> 00:06:46.961
abortion.

00:06:47.095 --> 00:06:48.563
The problem with that, that

00:06:48.696 --> 00:06:50.265
requires an actual visit tie

00:06:50.398 --> 00:06:52.166
clinic, whereas, medication

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.135
abortion can be done with

00:06:54.135 --> 00:06:54.302
telemedicine.

00:06:54.435 --> 00:06:56.271
Even folks driving from states

00:06:56.404 --> 00:06:58.139
where it's illegal, to states

00:06:58.239 --> 00:06:59.707
where it's legal, had the

00:07:00.141 --> 00:07:00.942
opportunity in recent months to

00:07:01.075 --> 00:07:03.745
cross the border, do a

00:07:04.145 --> 00:07:05.079
telemedicine visit from their

00:07:05.213 --> 00:07:05.513
car.

00:07:05.647 --> 00:07:07.382
And the hope was that they could

00:07:07.515 --> 00:07:09.150
fill it at a pharmacy, giving

00:07:09.284 --> 00:07:10.451
them access as well.

00:07:10.585 --> 00:07:11.686
That will be much more limited.

00:07:11.819 --> 00:07:13.354
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:07:13.488 --> 00:07:16.557
And, correct me if I'm wrong,

00:07:16.691 --> 00:07:19.093
but I believe mifepristone is

00:07:19.227 --> 00:07:20.628
approved and prescribed only to

00:07:20.762 --> 00:07:23.164
end the pregnancies through ten

00:07:23.298 --> 00:07:24.365
weeks.

00:07:24.499 --> 00:07:26.167
So, when people talk about using

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.469
it -- like, we're not talking

00:07:28.603 --> 00:07:30.171
about third trimester, so this

00:07:30.238 --> 00:07:33.308
is plaintiffs trying to -- am I

00:07:33.441 --> 00:07:33.608
wrong?

00:07:33.741 --> 00:07:34.208
Correct me if I'm wrong.

00:07:34.342 --> 00:07:39.447
&gt;&gt; No, you're completely

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:39.781
correct.

00:07:40.181 --> 00:07:43.418
It's fda approved to ten weeks

00:07:43.551 --> 00:07:44.852
used nationwide off of

00:07:44.986 --> 00:07:48.189
tremendous studies of efficacy

00:07:48.189 --> 00:07:49.457
to 11 weeks.

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:51.526
Now, the majority, vast

00:07:51.659 --> 00:07:53.528
majority, almost 90% of American

00:07:53.661 --> 00:07:54.495
abortions happen within that

00:07:54.629 --> 00:07:56.197
first trimester.

00:07:56.197 --> 00:07:58.199
So we're absolutely not talking

00:07:58.199 --> 00:08:00.201
second or third trimester

00:08:00.234 --> 00:08:00.468
abortions.

00:08:00.601 --> 00:08:02.203
But we are talking about the

00:08:02.203 --> 00:08:03.838
vast majority of abortions which

00:08:04.205 --> 00:08:05.373
happen in the first trimester.

00:08:05.506 --> 00:08:07.642
And half of those patients are

00:08:07.775 --> 00:08:09.210
choosing these drugs so they can

00:08:09.344 --> 00:08:10.211
do it at home.

